=base:summary.cmark

A whishlist, which actually is a todolist.

=base:main-content.cmark

- test and fix what we find on commonmark module
- port all .js to a single PureScript lib, deprecate histogram
- constellation mode/app to search/graph multiple kitchen-sinks
- load from elsewhere than disk
- support citation references
- consider listing/index of all code snippets,images,etc.
- hide zero-counts of links etc.
- new layouts: landing/marketing page (hero + feature grid + CTA), documentation layout with a persistent sidebar TOC, changelog/release-notes (grouped by version), portfolio/case-study, redirect/short-link page
- new sections: ~~callout/admonition~~, ~~FAQ/accordion~~, auto-derived table of contents, ~~pricing/comparison table~~, series/related-articles cross-linking

=base:callout.json
{"kind": "tip"
,"title": "New!"
,"body": "Callout/admonition sections just landed. This box is one, authored via a callout.json section interleaved with main-content sections; kind can be note, tip, warning, important/danger, or anything else (unstyled fallback). The body is plain text for now, no markdown rendering yet."
}

=base:main-content.cmark

Main-content and callout sections render in the order they appear in the source file, so authors can interleave prose and admonitions freely. Two more section types landed alongside callouts:

=base:faq.json
{"items":
  [ {"question": "Does a faq section support markdown in answers?", "answer": "Not yet, same plain-text limitation as callout bodies."}
  , {"question": "Can I have more than one faq section per article?", "answer": "Yes, they render in file order just like callouts and main-content."}
  ]
}

